    "n_emissionprocess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in emissionprocess."
    },
    "n_outputCohort": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 125,
      "description": "THE FIRST DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many cohorts reach MOVESOutput in each pollutant-process block. A cohort is a (sourceTypeID, fuelTypeID, modelYearID) triple -- `runspecsourcefueltype` is the grid's second factor and carries PAIRS -- so this number is a SUM over the run's source types and not a product: 125 at one source type (of 164 candidates, ragged by fuel: 41 gasoline model years, 40 diesel, 23 E85, 21 electricity), 248 at two (125 + 123) and 430 at five (41 + 125 + 125 + 89 + 50). WHICH candidates survive is a result of the chain (docs/mixed-onroad.md 2.2's `stmyFraction > 0` rule) and is never written down: `coh_rank` numbers the survivors 1..n by an inclusive prefix count over the candidate grid and the output row joins to that rank (docs/esm-conventions.md 22). `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes the number from the chain, `pp_selectedCohortCount` recomputes it separately for each pollutant-process, and tests pin all three together."
    },
    "n_outputPolProcess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 3,
      "description": "THE SECOND DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many of the run's selected pollutant-processes reach MOVESOutput at all. Three of three here, because every one of 9101, 10710 and 11710 has its rates on a road type this run selects. A run that selects start exhaust or extended idle on an on-road road type alone has fewer: those processes' rates live on the off-network road type 1, `BaseRateCalculator` joins its rate rows to `runSpecRoadType`, and the whole block is discarded (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.2). WHICH pollutant-processes survive is never written down -- `rspp_isEmitted` decides it from `emissionprocess.occursOnRealRoads` and `runspecroadtype`, `rspp_outputOrdinal` numbers the survivors 1..n by an inclusive prefix count, and `outputPolProcessCount` recomputes this number from the chain."
    },
    "n_sourceBin": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "THE THIRD DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many source bins the widest cohort of this run holds. A MOVES source bin is (sourceTypeID, fuelTypeID, modelYearID, regClassID, engTechID) and a cohort is only the first three of those, so one cohort can carry several bins -- `samplevehiclepopulation` gives a passenger car exactly one, a light commercial truck two (regulatory classes 30 and 41) and a refuse truck's diesel eight. The candidate grid needs a DENSE slot count and no table states this one, so it is declared and then CHECKED: `run_sourceBinsDropped` counts the bins a slot short of this would silently lose, and is asserted at 0. 1 is the value of every run that selects a source type whose cohorts are single-binned, which is every run in `runspecs/` before 7e."
    },
    "n_physicsRow": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "THE FOURTH DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many rows of `sourceusetypephysics` the run's source types select between them. The vehicle a drive cycle is computed for is keyed by (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range) and NOT by source type -- the national table holds 178 rows over 13 source types, one apiece for a motorcycle and a passenger car, three for a light commercial truck (regulatory class 30, and 41 split at model year 2010 because its fixed mass factor changes from 2.05979 to 5.0), fifteen for a refuse truck and twenty for a combination long-haul truck. The drive cycle is this document's largest relational step -- 63,602 drive-schedule seconds binned into operating modes, once per vehicle -- so its axis is the run's SELECTED physics rows densely ranked, and not the padded product of source types and a slot count that `n_sourceBin` can afford at cohort scale. No table states the number, so it is declared and then CHECKED both ways: `run_physicsRowsSelected` recomputes it from the chain and `run_physicsRowsDropped` counts the selected rows that fall past it, which is asserted at 0. 1 is the value of every run in `runspecs/`, 4 for source types 21 and 32 together, 40 for the five of `expand-sourcetype`."
    },
    "n_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecpollutantprocess. The FIRST factor of both the rate relation and the output relation: three pollutant-processes here, and a run selecting one more would size both relations differently with no other edit."
    },
    "n_runspecchainedto": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecchainedto."
    },
    "n_pm10emissionratio": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in pm10emissionratio."
    },
    "n_sourceusetypephysics": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in sourceUseTypePhysics."
    }
  },
