        "zmh_heatIndex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "degF",
          "shape": [
            "zonemonthhour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`ZoneMonthHour.heatIndex`, COMPUTED from `temperature` and `relHumidity` rather than read back off the reference: MeteorologyGenerator.doHeatIndex MG-3, ported as lib/meteorology.esm's `heat_index` and specified in docs/meteorology-generator.md 2.2. It is the dry-bulb temperature below 78 degF and the National Weather Service regression capped at 120 degF at or above it, and the branch is not decoration -- over this snapshot's own 24 hours the regression runs 1.80 to 6.25 degF above the temperature on the 17 hours it is not used on.\n\nThe run's hour is 7, at 59.500000000000 degF, so what reaches `run_heatIndex` is the sub-78 arm and the computed value is the temperature BIT FOR BIT, which is why this retarget moves not one byte of this fixture's MOVESOutput (docs/esm-conventions.md 23, docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2). Over all 24 rows the computed column agrees with the reference's stored one to 7.93e-15 relative, 17 of them bit-identical."
        },
