          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S3's denominator, over every (source type, age) in THIS source type's HPMS group and not only this source type. Normalising over source type 21 alone is a 2.55x error on every row."
        },
        "run_monthGroupID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J29's key: August is month group 8."
        },
        "run_heatIndex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "degF",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The heat index at the run's hour, PER COUNTY, and the number both of this chain's clamps turn on. In `process-tirewear` and `expand-day` there is one and it is 59.500000000000 degF -- hour 7, where the temperature is 59.5 and the sub-78 arm of MG-3 returns it unchanged. In `expand-counties` there are three and they differ, which is the point. It is now COMPUTED by `zmh_heatIndex` rather than read off `ZoneMonthHour.heatIndex`, and because that arm is an identity the computed value is the ingested one bit for bit.\n\nTHE TWO MARGINS, both measured against this snapshot's own `monthgrouphour` row (A -3.63154, B 0.072465, C -0.000276): the A/C activity quadratic crosses 0 at a heat index of 67.4340633418 degF, so 59.5 is 7.934 degF below the clamp; the EV suppression fires above 67.0 degF, so 59.5 is 7.500 degF below it. The prose here used to say 66.900001525879 with margins of 0.3 and 0.1 degF. That is `mixed-onroad`'s hour 9, not this fixture's hour 7 -- a claim copied across documents, contradicted by this file's own `the_run_scope` assertion of 59.5 and by docs/process-tirewear.md 7.3's \"59.5 is 7.5 degF below\". docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 carries the margin table for all eight retargeted fixtures."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermA": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s constant term, read from monthgrouphour. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermB": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/degF",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s linear term. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityTermC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/degF^2",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15(d)'s quadratic term. Constant across the run's counties, and shaped over them anyway: it is ADDED to a per-county heat index, and broadcasting it here is cheaper to read than an aggregate at every use."
        },
        "run_acActivityRaw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "setup.rs:409 before the clamp, in Horner form as the canonical SQL writes it: A + h(B + Ch), per county. -0.0189 at `process-tirewear`'s single county."
        },
        "run_acActivity": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "setup.rs:411's clamp(0, 1), which makes it exactly 0 in every run this document has been asked for -- in each of `expand-counties`' three counties as well, so the non-zero A/C arm still has no fixture (§23). Written out rather than factored into a `clamp01` template, because §4.8 argues the VALUE each of this chain's two clamps takes is the load-bearing fact and a shared template would hide which is which."
        },
        "run_evTemperatureIsSuppressed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "adjust.rs:114's `sourceTypeID < 40 && heatIndex > 67.0`. FALSE by one tenth of a degree in the one-county runs, and evaluated per county."
        },
        "run_brakingOpModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The Braking operating mode, NAMED. It was a bare literal 0 until finding F32 was fixed upstream -- an `enums` value had to be a positive integer and MOVES's Braking mode is genuinely 0, so the one mode this document most needed to name was the one it could not. A constant equality is still a join.on (docs/esm-conventions.md §20.4), so this one-row column is what the two braking-rate lookups key on."
        },
        "run_brakeRate1Sec": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "-2 mph/s, READ from the Braking row of operatingmode rather than written into drivecycle.rs's own literal."
        },
        "run_brakeRate3Sec": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "-1 mph/s, the three-consecutive-seconds threshold."
        },
        "run_physicsRowsSelected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many physics rows the run's source types select between them, recomputed from the chain so `n_physicsRow` is a CHECKED declaration and not a transcription. 1 for a run that selects a motorcycle or a passenger car alone, 4 for source types 21 and 32 together, 40 for the five of `expand-sourcetype`. It was a per-source-type count until 7d-next, and a test pinned it at 1 because until then the only alternative to one row was a wrong answer."
        },
        "run_physicsRowsDropped": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many selected physics rows fall past `n_physicsRow` and are therefore not on the drive-cycle axis at all. It is the check on the fourth declared number and it is the same KIND of check as `run_sourceBinsDropped`: a short axis is not a missing output row but a rate row that finds no vehicle, so its meanBaseRate is 0 and the cohort's quantity is quietly low by that regulatory class's share. Zero is the only passing value."
        },
        "run_rateRowsWithoutPhysics": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many SELECTED rate rows find no vehicle -- no `sourceusetypephysics` row with the bin's source type and regulatory class covering the bin's model year. It is the other half of `run_physicsRowsDropped`: that one catches an axis too short for the rows that exist, this one catches a rate row whose regulatory class the physics table never had. In the default database every (source type, regulatory class) pair `samplevehiclepopulation` carries has a physics row covering every model year of it, so zero is the value AND the assertion."
        },
        "run_fuelUsageWildcardCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many fuelusagefraction rows carry modelYearGroupID 0. All five, which licenses the rebase omitting that key pair: source_bin_distribution_generator.rs:1547 makes 0 a wildcard, and a row with a real group would need a predicate this document does not carry."
        },
        "cohortSurvivorCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The cohort total, computed from the chain, so `n_outputCohort` is a CHECKED declaration rather than a transcription. 125 at one source type and the SUM over them at more."
        },
        "run_sourceBinsDropped": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many source bins of a SELECTED cohort fall past slot `n_sourceBin` and are therefore not in the candidate grid at all. It is the check on the third declared number, and it is a different kind of check from the other two: `cohortSurvivorCount` and `outputPolProcessCount` recompute a declaration that is only ever too big or too small by a row, while a slot count that is one short drops a whole rate and its emissions with it, silently and low. Zero is the only passing value."
        },
        "outputPolProcessCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "3, computed from the chain, so `n_outputPolProcess` is a CHECKED declaration rather than a transcription -- the companion of `cohortSurvivorCount` on the other output axis."
        },
