          "description": "The run's drive-cycle relation: one row per (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range) the run's source types select, in `sourceusetypephysics` order. At `n_physicsRow` 1 it is the one vehicle a single-regulatory-class source type has, and the chain below it is what it was before the axis existed."
        },
        "phy_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The vehicle's source type. A drive schedule is associated with a source type and an average-speed distribution is keyed by one, so this is how the per-source-type half of the drive cycle reaches the per-vehicle half."
