          "description": "Which of the run's source types the vehicle belongs to, as the ordinal the per-source-type relations are laid out by. The drive cycle has two halves -- the schedules and speed brackets, which are per (source type, road type), and the operating-mode binning, which is per vehicle -- and this is the join between them."
        },
        "ds_firstSecond": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_schedule_rows"
          ],
          "description": "drivecycle.rs:203-206: a schedule's first second is its MINIMUM second, not zero and not row zero. Reached through the 49-row schedule table rather than by a min over the 63,602-row relation joined to itself -- the same answer at 1300x the leaf count."
