        "outSourceTypeOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output row's source type, as a rank into `runspecsourcetype_rows`, read BACK through the same ordinal join every other output column uses. `out_SHO` needs it because the activity relation is now per source type. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point."
        },
