            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output row's source type, read BACK through the rank join like every other key column. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point."
