            }
          }
        },
        "zmh_temperature": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "degF",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "zonemonthhour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "zonemonthhour.temperature, 59.5 degF at hour 7. The temperature adjustment reads THIS column and the A/C activity term and the EV suppression read `zmh_heatIndex`; the two are equal on the 17 of this snapshot's 24 hours that are below 78 degF -- hour 7 among them -- and differ by up to 1.6 degF on the other seven, so the distinction costs nothing at THIS hour and is made because adjust.rs:495-535 makes it.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_zonemonthhour",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "temperature"
            }
          }
        },
        "zmh_relHumidity": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "percent",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "zonemonthhour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "zonemonthhour.relHumidity, in PERCENT and not as a fraction -- 90.400001525879 at hour 7. It is the second argument of the heat-index regression and it is read for no other purpose here; below 78 degF the regression is not evaluated at all, so on this fixture's own hour the column is ingested and then not used, which is exactly why `zmh_heatIndex` is asserted over hours the branch DOES reach.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_zonemonthhour",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "relHumidity"
            }
          }
        },
        "rspp_ordinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant-process relation's own row ordinal, so the rate and output relations join to it by position."
        },
        "rspp_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant half of the packed identifier: 91, 107, 117."
        },
        "rspp_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The process half: 1 (Running Exhaust) and 10 (Tirewear)."
        },
        "rspp_occursOnRealRoads": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether this pollutant-process's rates live on a real road, looked up from `emissionprocess` by its process half. 1 on all three here."
        },
        "rspp_rateRoadTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The road type this pollutant-process's rates are written on. `BaseRateGenerator` emits a real-road process on every road type the RunSpec selected and an off-network one on road type 1 alone, so this is the run's road type or the OffNetwork enum's 1 -- 4, 4 and 4 here."
        },
        "rspp_isEmitted": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether this pollutant-process produces output rows at all: `BaseRateCalculator` joins its rate rows to `runSpecRoadType` (baseratecalculator/mod.rs:762-781), so a block whose rate road type the RunSpec did not select is discarded entire. 1, 1, 1 here and 1, 0, 0 for a run that selects 9101, 9102 and 9190 on road type 4, where the 250 rows MOVES writes are the running-exhaust block alone (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.2)."
        },
        "rspp_emittedPrefix": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "An inclusive prefix count of the emission mask over the pollutant-process relation: how many at or before this one are emitted. The same construction `coh_prefixSelected` uses one axis down (docs/esm-conventions.md 22)."
        },
        "rspp_outputOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which output block this pollutant-process owns, numbered 1..n_outputPolProcess over the emitted ones and 0 for a discarded one -- an ordinal no output row can match. 1, 2, 3 here."
        },
        "rspp_usesAvgSpeedModes": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which generator wrote this pollutant-process's `RatesOpModeDistribution`, and therefore which operating-mode family its weights live on. It is a PROCESS test because the reference makes it one on both sides: `BaseRateGenerator` drives the drive cycles itself only for processes 1 and 9 (mod.rs:156-161) and `AverageSpeedOperatingModeDistributionGenerator` handles process 10 and errors out for anything else (avg_speed_op_mode_distribution.rs:110-116, and its executeLoop logs 'AvgSpeedOMDG called for unknown process'). Both constants are ported as enum members rather than as digits. 0 on the 9101 row and 1 on both tire-wear rows."
        },
        "rspp_isEnergy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether S18's kilojoule-to-MillionBTU conversion applies. engine.rs:1286-1310 applies it to pollutants 91, 92 and 93 and to nothing else, so the two tire-wear pollutants stay in grams. The membership rule is lib/onroad_activity.esm's `is_energy_pollutant` rather than three inline comparisons, and 92 and 93 are named there even though this run selects neither."
        },
        "rspp_unitDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The divisor S18 applies after the group-by sum: 1,055,055.9 kJ per Million BTU for an energy pollutant and exactly 1 for a mass one."
        },
        "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "A LEFT JOIN onto runspecchainedto: 11710 for the chained 10710 and 0 -- the additive identity, which is no pollutant-process -- for the two that carry a rate of their own. That 0 is what makes the chain term vanish on an unchained row without a branch."
        },
        "ppmy_shortModYrGroupID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "pollutantprocessmodelyear_rows"
          ],
          "description": "modelyeargroup.shortModYrGroupID resolved AT the pollutantprocessmodelyear row. It has to be here rather than on the cohort because a join key column must be one-dimensional, and the cohort's short group depends on the pollutant-process as well: 9101 maps model year 2020 to short group 40 (a two-digit year) and 11710 maps every model year to 0, modelYearGroup 0's \"Doesn't Matter\". Same cohort, different source bin -- and a third encoding beside brake wear's decade bands."
        },
        "rt_ordinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The rate relation's own row ordinal. The relation is the n_runspecpollutantprocess pollutant-processes crossed with the n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype cohort candidate grid -- 3 x 164 = 492 rows, every factor a DISCOVERED extent. It exists because everything the base rate needs is keyed by BOTH, and a join key column has to be one-dimensional (docs/esm-conventions.md 2: tables stay tables)."
        },
        "rt_polProcOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which pollutant-process this rate row is for. Pollutant-process major, so each one occupies a contiguous run of 164 rows."
        },
        "rt_outputBlockOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output block this rate row's pollutant-process owns, read back from `rspp_outputOrdinal`. 0 on every row of a discarded pollutant-process, which is what keeps `rt_outputOrdinal` from matching anything."
        },
        "rt_binOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which source-bin candidate this rate row is for. The rate relation is the pollutant-process crossed with the BIN and not with the cohort, because every rate lookup below it keys on a regulatory class, an engine technology or both: `emissionrate` on all five bin columns, `temperatureadjustment` and `evefficiency` on the regulatory class, `fleetavgadjustment` on the group it belongs to."
        },
        "rt_cohortOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "And which cohort that bin belongs to -- the key the output rank is built on, and the one the key columns and the activity join use."
        },
        "rt_polProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant-process this rate row carries."
        },
        "rt_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its pollutant."
        },
        "rt_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its process."
        },
