          "description": "S14 (J26): the operating mode is contracted away against the weights of THIS RATE ROW'S OWN pollutant-process, reached through J41. This is `baserate_1_2020.meanBaseRate` on the energy rows and `baserate_10_2020.meanBaseRate` on the tire-wear ones, computed rather than read -- and the two are collapsed against DIFFERENT weight vectors: 23 drive-cycle modes for 9101 and 16 speed-bin modes for 11710. The two rate tables are seven orders of magnitude apart, 392,141 kJ per source-hour against 0.0000197 g, so a wrong weight is a wrong number in every cell. Per county, through the same rebase. THE WEIGHTS ARE THIS RATE ROW'S OWN VEHICLE'S as of 7d-next, reached through `rt_physicsOrdinal` rather than through the source type: a light commercial truck's regulatory class 30 and its regulatory class 41 have different fixed mass factors, so their drive-schedule seconds bin into different operating modes and the same rate table collapses to two different numbers."
