        "rtDay_quantChained": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "PM10BrakeTireCalculator's whole arithmetic: the PM2.5 sibling's quantity, at the SAME cohort and day, times the PM10/PM2.5 ratio. It is a SELF-JOIN of the rate relation -- the chained row and the row it is chained from are two rows of one relation -- so the clause names its two sides with `syms` (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.5.8). On an unchained row the ratio is 0 and the chain key is 0, which matches no pollutant-process, so both halves say the same thing. Per county."
