        {
          "_comment": "THE FOUR NEIGHBOURING-SECOND READS finding F11 used to refuse. Each is `driveschedulesecond` joined to ITSELF -- two ranges over one index set -- on (offset second, driveScheduleID), with `syms` naming which side each key column is read at. The offset pair is written FIRST because the driving clause is the first one the evaluator can resolve and its selectivity is the runtime (docs/esm-conventions.md §25): the second key is 3.2 rows per value where the schedule key is 1,298. Measured on this document: 63,602 rows and 4.045e9 candidate pairs per join, eight joins, and the whole W stage evaluates in about two seconds.",
