          "_comment": "S12, source_bin_distribution_generator.rs:1590-1637, and it IS a self-join: the used row and the equipped row are two rows of the same candidate relation. `syms` names which side each key column is read at. Since 7e the two sides agree on the SOURCE BIN -- source type, model year, engine technology and regulatory class -- and differ only in the fuel, which is what MOVES's `sourceBinFuelUsage` remap is; before 7e the engine technology and the regulatory class were sums over a cohort's rows and the pairing held only where each cohort had one row. mixed-onroad also paired `coh_modelYearGroupID`; that column is a property of the pollutant-process as well as of the cohort and lives on the rate relation, and the pair was redundant anyway because the model year is joined beside it.",
