        {
          "id": "the_short_model_year_group_is_a_property_of_the_pollutant_process",
          "description": "The one cohort key that differs between the two rate paths, and the reason the rate relation exists at all. `pollutantprocessmodelyear` maps model year 2020 to modelYearGroup 2020 for 9101, whose `shortModYrGroupID` is 40 -- a two-digit year -- and model year 1980 to 80. For 11710 it maps EVERY model year to modelYearGroup 0, whose `modelyeargroup` row is named \"Doesn't Matter\" and whose short group is 0, and all 31 of `emissionrate`'s 11710 source bins carry 00 in that slot. So tire wear's encoding is neither brake wear's decade bands nor running exhaust's two-digit years but a third thing -- a constant -- and a document that computed one short group per COHORT would read the 527 tire-wear rate rows with a source bin of 40 or 80 and produce a tire-wear rate of exactly zero. Same defect as brake wear's, reached by a different encoding, which is why the fix is structural rather than a special case.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
