        {
          "id": "the_PM10_chain_is_a_ratio_lookup_and_here_it_is_a_single_constant",
          "description": "PM10BrakeTireCalculator, entirely, on the tire-wear edge. `pm10emissionratio` carries four rows here -- one per fuel type, polProcessID 10710, model years 1940-2060 -- and all four hold the SAME 6.6667. The ratio is 0 on the two unchained rate paths, because the table carries 10710 and nothing else, and that zero is what makes `rtDay_quantChained` vanish there without a branch. `rtDay_quantDirect` is asserted at exactly 0 on a chained row for the mirror reason: `emissionrate` has no 10710 row, so J22's inner join leaves its rate at the additive identity and the chained block's whole quantity comes through the chain.\n\nTHIS IS A WEAKER CHECK OF THE LOOKUP THAN process-brakewear's, AND SAYING SO IS THE POINT (docs/esm-conventions.md 23). There the eight rows were two model-year ranges over four fuels carrying three distinct values, so dropping the range predicate was a factor of three and dropping the fuel key was 83 %. Here a document that dropped BOTH would still reproduce all 250 PM10 rows. What these assertions can still see is that the ratio is looked up per rate row rather than hoisted to the run -- 0 on the unchained paths and 6.6667 on the chained one -- and docs/process-tirewear.md 7.2 records that the discriminating half of the join is checked by `process-brakewear` and by nothing here.",
